{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The חֲסִידָה.</b> This is a white kite — ציגוני\"א. And why is its name חֲסִידָה? Because it does kindness with its companions in food (ibid.)." "<b>The אֲנָפָה.</b> It is an irascible kite. And it seems to me that they call it הי\"רון." "<b>The דּוּכִיפַת.</b> A wild rooster, and its crest is doubled, and in לַעַז הרופ\"א. And why is its name דּוּכִיפַת? Because 'its glory is folded' — and that is its crest. And נַגַּר טוּרָא is called by its name on account of its deeds, as our Sages explained in tractate Gittin, chapter 'One who was seized' (Gittin 68a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "the la'az ציגוני\"א is Old French cigogne, 'stork'", 1 "the la'az הי\"רון is likely Old French hairon, 'heron'", 2 "the la'az הרופ\"א is Old French herupe or huppe, 'hoopoe'; נַגַּר טוּרָא appears to be an Aramaic phrase meaning 'mountain carpenter'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:53.673861240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}